            <div xml:id="d816">

                <pb facs="0766" n="760" sameAs="frus:frus1939v04/pg760"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">867N.01/1558: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Geneva</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Bucknell</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1939-05-22T22:00:00+01:00">May 22, 1939—10
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received May 22—8:47 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>143. In a statement on Palestine in the Council this afternoon<anchor n="72"
                        xml:id="d816-f1"/> the British representative stated that the recent White
                    Paper would be circulated to members of the Council and that he would not go
                    into details of British plan until opportunity had been had to examine document
                    in detail. A full opportunity for discussion would be given at a later session
                    of the Council after the measure had been debated by the British Parliament.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bucknell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
